  [1mWhat changes[0m

  - [1mEvent type: checkboxes instead of a Select.[0m A list of the nine real types in a fieldset titled "Event types". With
    nothing ticked, all events show. I'm switching because "security changes" covers several types, which a
    single-choice Select can't do.
  - [1mTwo shortcut buttons above it:[0m "Failed sign-ins" and "Security changes".
    - Each one ticks exactly its real types and unticks the rest.
    - The filter is always a visible set of real event types, so I'm not inventing a client-side category.
    - "Security changes" would tick Password changed, Two-factor enabled and Email change requested.
  - [1mDate range: added, per the 03-forms pattern.[0m A presets Select ("Any time", "Last 7 days", "Last 30 days", "Custom
    range") plus From and To date fields.
    - Dates are whole days in your own time zone and include both ends, so a particular week is From Monday, To Sunday.
    - If To is before From, an inline error appears when you leave the field and the date filter isn't applied. Nothing
      is checked while you type.
  - [1mAll filters combine.[0m The live count and the "Clear filters" button cover all of them.
  - [1mSize:[0m about 250–300 lines including [38;5;153mtokens.css[39m. If it goes past 300, I'll stop and propose a split.

  One thing to confirm: I've left "Settings updated" out of security changes, because the sample data only shows it for
  notification preferences ([38;5;153mnotifyDigest[39m). Say if it should be in.

  Is the revised design approved?

